<title>DUBAI: Saudi Aramco cuts bunker fuel prices.</title>
<headline>Saudi Aramco cuts bunker fuel prices.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-06-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Aramco has cut A-960 bunker fuel by $2 a tonne to $102 ($15.66 a barrel) from Ras Tanura and Damman and to $98.50 ($15.04) for Jeddah and Yanbu exports, Aramco said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>A-888 bunker diesel from the Gulf ports is cut by $3 a tonne to $206 and by $10 a tonne to $179 from the Red Sea ports.</p>
<p>Prices are effective June 12.</p>
